  "guide": {
    "intro": [
      "Daoism is both a philosophy and a religion. As philosophy, it asks you to live in harmony with the Dao, the way things naturally unfold. As religion, it includes temples, priests, and long traditions of inner alchemy and healing.",
      "Its two great early texts are the Tao Te Ching and the Zhuangzi. They are poetic, playful and hard to pin down on purpose."
    ],
